   <title><![CDATA[Ep. 186: A Light on the Hill: Faith, Politics, and the Legacy of Capitol Hill Baptist [The Outstanding Podcast]]]></title>
   <link/>
   <description><![CDATA[<p class="e-9652-text encore-text-body-medium" data-encore-id="text" data-slate-node="element"><span data-slate-node="text"><span class="sc-iAJcmt kMXkFi" data-slate-leaf="true">Should faith and politics mix? Joseph Backholm sits down with Caleb Morrell, author of&nbsp;</span></span><span data-slate-node="text"><span class="sc-iAJcmt kMXkFi" data-slate-leaf="true"><em>A Light on the Hill</em></span></span><span data-slate-node="text"><span class="sc-iAJcmt kMXkFi" data-slate-leaf="true">, to explore the unique role of Capitol Hill Baptist Church in shaping evangelicalism in the nation&rsquo;s capital. Caleb shares his journey with the church, uncovering its rich 150-year history, from its founding to its enduring biblical foundation despite cultural shifts. They discuss the church&rsquo;s impact in political spaces, the significance of strong leadership, and how it has remained a guiding light through changing times.</span></span></p>
